#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:4
msgid "Signing packages with Sigstore (Cosign)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:6
msgid ""
"This is an example of a package signing plugin implementation using "
"`Sigstore <https://www.sigstore.dev/>`_ via `Cosign <https://github.com/"
"sigstore/cosign>`_. You need **Cosign** (version 3.0.0 or newer) on your "
"``PATH``. See the `Cosign releases <https://github.com/sigstore/cosign/"
"releases>`_ page for binaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../common/experimental_warning.inc:3
msgid ""
"This feature is experimental and subject to breaking changes. See :ref:`the "
"Conan stability<stability>` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:14
msgid ""
"This example is available in the examples2 repository: `examples/extensions/"
"plugins/sigstore_sign <https://github.com/conan-io/examples2/tree/main/"
"examples/extensions/plugins/sigstore_sign>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:18
msgid ""
"Cosign is used here for demonstration only. The package signing plugin "
"mechanism is backend-agnostic; you could implement a similar plugin with "
"other tools (for example OpenSSL or GPG) by changing the commands invoked "
"from ``sign()`` and ``verify()``, as described in :ref:"
"`reference_extensions_package_signing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:24
msgid "Generating the signing key pair"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:26
msgid ""
"Generate a Cosign key pair (Cosign prompts for a passphrase to protect the "
"private key):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:28
msgid "$ cosign generate-key-pair --output-key-prefix signing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:32
msgid ""
"This creates ``signing.key`` (private) and ``signing.pub`` (public). Use the "
"passphrase later to set the ``COSIGN_PASSWORD`` environment variable when "
"configuring the plugin (see below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:37
msgid "Configuring the plugin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:41
msgid ""
"This example stores a private key next to the plugin for simplicity. **Do "
"not do this in production.** Instead, load the signing key from environment "
"variables or a secret manager, or delegate signing to a remote signing "
"service. **Always keep the private key out of the Conan cache and out of "
"source control**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:45
msgid ""
"Copy ``sign.py`` and ``signing-config.json`` from the examples2 folder into "
"your Conan home:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:47
msgid "``CONAN_HOME/extensions/plugins/sign/sign.py``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:49
msgid "``CONAN_HOME/extensions/plugins/sign/signing-config.json``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:51
msgid ""
"Place the generated keys in a folder named after the **provider** used by "
"the plugin. This example uses ``my-organization`` (the name is hardcoded in "
"``sign.py``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:54
msgid "``CONAN_HOME/extensions/plugins/sign/my-organization/signing.key``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:56
msgid "``CONAN_HOME/extensions/plugins/sign/my-organization/signing.pub``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:58
msgid ""
"Set the ``COSIGN_PASSWORD`` environment variable. The plugin **requires** "
"this variable to be present when signing: Cosign reads it instead of "
"prompting on the terminal. Set it to the **private key passphrase** you "
"chose when generating the key pair. If the key has **no** passphrase, set "
"``COSIGN_PASSWORD`` to an empty value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:62
msgid "Your layout should look like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:64
msgid ""
"CONAN_HOME/\n"
"└── extensions/\n"
"    └── plugins/\n"
"        └── sign/\n"
"            ├── sign.py\n"
"            ├── signing-config.json\n"
"            └── my-organization/\n"
"                ├── signing.key\n"
"                └── signing.pub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:79
msgid ""
"The package signing plugin lives under the Conan configuration directory, so "
"you can distribute it with :ref:`conan config "
"install<reference_commands_conan_config_install>` (for example from a fork "
"or internal repo that contains the same files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:85
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:89
msgid ""
"**Method name convention:** Use the literal string ``sigstore`` (lowercase) "
"in the ``method`` field when your plugin uses this Cosign/Sigstore tools. "
"This is a convenient way to identify the signing method used to sign the "
"package and so the verifier can pick the right backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:93
msgid ""
"For signing, ``sign()`` invokes :command:`cosign sign-blob` on Conan's "
"``pkgsign-manifest.json``, writes a Sigstore **bundle** (``artifact.sigstore."
"json``) next to the manifest, and returns metadata for ``pkgsign-signatures."
"json``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:96
msgid ""
"def sign(ref, artifacts_folder, signature_folder, **kwargs):\n"
"    ...\n"
"    cosign_sign_cmd = [\n"
"        \"cosign\",\n"
"        \"sign-blob\",\n"
"        \"--key\",\n"
"        privkey_filepath,\n"
"        \"--bundle\",\n"
"        bundle_filepath,\n"
"        \"-y\",\n"
"        f\"--signing-config={_signing_config_path()}\",\n"
"        manifest_filepath,\n"
"    ]\n"
"    try:\n"
"        _run_command(cosign_sign_cmd)\n"
"        ConanOutput().success(f\"Package signed for reference {ref}\")\n"
"    except Exception as exc:\n"
"        raise ConanException(f\"Error signing artifact: {exc}\") from exc\n"
"\n"
"    return [\n"
"        {\n"
"            \"method\": \"sigstore\",\n"
"            \"provider\": provider,\n"
"            \"sign_artifacts\": {\n"
"                \"manifest\": \"pkgsign-manifest.json\",\n"
"                \"bundle\": \"artifact.sigstore.json\",\n"
"            },\n"
"        }\n"
"    ]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:128
msgid ""
"For verification, ``verify()`` reads ``pkgsign-signatures.json``, resolves "
"the manifest and bundle paths, loads the public key for the recorded "
"**provider**, and runs :command:`cosign verify-blob` (without Rekor support):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:131
msgid ""
"def verify(ref, artifacts_folder, signature_folder, files, **kwargs):\n"
"    ...\n"
"    cosign_verify_cmd = [\n"
"        \"cosign\",\n"
"        \"verify-blob\",\n"
"        \"--key\",\n"
"        pubkey_filepath,\n"
"        \"--bundle\",\n"
"        bundle_filepath,\n"
"        \"--private-infrastructure=true\",\n"
"        manifest_filepath,\n"
"    ]\n"
"    try:\n"
"        _run_command(cosign_verify_cmd)\n"
"        ConanOutput().success(f\"Package verified for reference {ref}\")\n"
"    except Exception as exc:\n"
"        raise ConanException(f\"Error verifying signature {bundle_filepath}: "
"{exc}\") from exc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:151
msgid ""
"If verification fails, the plugin raises ``ConanException``. On success it "
"does not return a value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:153
msgid ""
"You can read more about ``pkgsign-manifest.json`` at :ref:"
"`reference_extensions_package_signing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:157
msgid "Signing packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:159
msgid "Create a package and sign it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:161
msgid ""
"$ conan new cmake_lib -d name=hello -d version=1.0\n"
"$ conan create\n"
"$ conan cache sign hello/1.0\n"
"\n"
"hello/1.0: Compressing conan_sources.tgz\n"
"hello/1.0:dee9f7f985eb1c20e3c41afaa8c35e2a34b5ae0b: Compressing "
"conan_package.tgz\n"
"Running command: cosign sign-blob --key .../sign/my-organization/signing.key "
"--bundle .../metadata/sign/artifact.sigstore.json -y --signing-config=.../"
"sign/signing-config.json .../metadata/sign/pkgsign-manifest.json\n"
"Package signed for reference hello/1.0\n"
"...\n"
"[Package sign] Summary: OK=2, FAILED=0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:176
msgid ""
"Starting with Conan 2.26.0, :command:`conan upload` does not sign packages "
"automatically. Use :command:`conan cache sign` before upload when remotes "
"should store signatures. See :ref:`reference_extensions_package_signing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:181
msgid "Verifying packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:183
msgid "Verify recipe and package binaries in the cache:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../examples/extensions/package_signing/package_signing_with_sigstore.rst:185
msgid ""
"$ conan cache verify hello/1.0\n"
"\n"
"[Package sign] Checksum verified for file conan_sources.tgz (...)\n"
"...\n"
"Running command: cosign verify-blob --key .../sign/my-organization/signing."
"pub --bundle .../metadata/sign/artifact.sigstore.json --private-"
"infrastructure=true .../metadata/sign/pkgsign-manifest.json\n"
"Package verified for reference hello/1.0\n"
"...\n"
"[Package sign] Summary: OK=2, FAILED=0"
msgstr ""

